  {"id":"cf-y2m8-10","set":"cfY2M8","topic":"Further kinematics","chapters":["ch:me2c8"],"num":"1","source":"P32 2021 Q1","marks":4,"year":2,"pageFrom":24,"pageTo":24,"msFrom":25,"msTo":25,"msCheck":"verified","flags":"","text":"1. A particle P moves with constant acceleration (2i − 3j) m s−2\n    At time t = 0, P is moving with velocity 4i m s−1\n    (a) Find the velocity of P at time t = 2 seconds.\n                                                                                                                  \n(2)\n    At time t = 0, the position vector of P relative to a fixed origin O is (i + j) m.\n    (b) Find the position vector of P relative to O at time t = 3 seconds.\n                                                                                                                  \n(2)\n2\n                  "},
  {"id":"cf-y2m8-11","set":"cfY2M8","topic":"Further kinematics","chapters":["ch:me2c8"],"num":"5","source":"P32 2021 Q5","marks":14,"year":2,"pageFrom":26,"pageTo":26,"msFrom":27,"msTo":28,"msCheck":"verified","flags":"","text":"5. At time t seconds, a particle P has velocity v m s−1, where\n                 1\n    v = 3t 2  i − 2t j    t > 0\n    (a) Find the acceleration of P at time t seconds, where t > 0\n                                                                                                                  \n(2)\n    (b) Find the value of t at the instant when P is moving in the direction of i − j\n                                                                                                                  \n(3)\n    At time t seconds, where t > 0, the position vector of P, relative to a fixed origin O,\n    is r metres.\n    When t = 1, r = −j\n    (c) Find an expression for r in terms of t.\n                                                                                                                  \n(3)\n    (d) Find the exact distance of P from O at the instant when P is moving with\n         speed 10 m s−1\n                                                                                                                  \n(6)\n16\n                                                                "},
  {"id":"cf-y2m8-12","set":"cfY2M8","topic":"Further kinematics","chapters":["ch:me2c8"],"num":"1","source":"P32 2022 Q1","marks":8,"year":2,"pageFrom":29,"pageTo":29,"msFrom":30,"msTo":30,"msCheck":"verified","flags":"","text":"1.     [In this question, position vectors are given relative to a fixed origin.]\n       At time t seconds, where  t > 0 , a particle P has velocity v m s–1 where\n                              1\n       v = 3t2i – 6t 2 j\n    (a) Find the speed of P at time t = 2 seconds.\n                                                                                                                  \n(2)\n    (b) Find an expression, in terms of t, i and j, for the acceleration of P at time t seconds,\n         where   t > 0\n                                                                                                                  \n(2)\n    At time t = 4 seconds, the position vector of P is (i – 4j) m.\n    (c) Find the position vector of P at time  t = 1 second.\n                                                                                                                  \n(4)\n    2\n                                                                                   "},
  {"id":"cf-y2m8-13","set":"cfY2M8","topic":"Further kinematics","chapters":["ch:me2c8"],"num":"3","source":"P32 2022 Q3","marks":9,"year":2,"pageFrom":31,"pageTo":31,"msFrom":32,"msTo":33,"msCheck":"verified","flags":"","text":"3.                        [In this question, i and j are horizontal unit vectors.]\n       A particle P of mass 4 kg is at rest at the point A on a smooth horizontal plane.\n       At time t = 0, two forces,  F1 = (4i – j) N  and   F2 = (λi + μj) N , where λ and μ are\n       constants, are applied to P\n       Given that P moves in the direction of the vector  (3i + j)\n       (a) show that\n                          λ – 3μ + 7 = 0\n                                                                                    \n(4)\n       At time  t = 4 seconds, P passes through the point B.\n       Given that  λ = 2\n    (b) find the length of AB.\n                                                                                                                  \n(5)\n    8\n                                                                                                "}
